    "durationMs": 105529,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and fully tested. I built it from scratch in `/workspace` with Express 4.21.2, Knex, and pg:\n\n- **`src/app.js`** — all routes: `POST /links` (201 with `{code, url, clicks: 0}`, submitted URL echoed unchanged, 409 on duplicate custom code, collision-safe generated codes), `GET /links` (ascending creation order with `total`), `GET /links/{code}` (200/404), and `GET /r/{code}` (302 with Location set directly from the stored URL, atomic `clicks + 1` so concurrent redirects increment exactly once each). Malformed JSON, invalid/missing URL, and invalid codes (4-20 ASCII letters/digits/hyphens/underscores) all return 422 with an `error` field.\n- **`src/db.js` + `knexfile.js` + `migrations/`** — connection string read from `DATABASE_URL`, nothing hard-coded; a `links` table with unique `code`, `url`, `clicks`, and creation order via auto-increment id.\n- **`start.sh`** (executable) — applies pending migrations with `knex migrate:latest`, then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`.\n- **`README.md`** — includes a \"Start the server\" section.\n\nI verified behavior with a 41-assertion curl suite (all passing), including a 20-way concurrent redirect race ending at exactly 20 clicks, then killed and restarted the server to confirm all links and click counts survive restarts. The test server is stopped and the workspace is clean."
  }
